claire: opened a small PR to consolidate streaming resume patterns + 429/timeouts/context-limit guidance. includes minimal node/python snippets and a tiny repro harness. PTAL :wave:

raj: link? want to check importer placement and snippet shape so it matches SDK quickstart conventions.

claire: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/900. harness is under examples/diagnostics/stream-resume-lite (no external deps, uses mock server).

marta: quick content ask: we should be explicit about what customers actually see for mid-stream failures (client abort vs server crash vs overload). ops keeps asking.

claire: added a compact matrix: sync 429 -> request rejected; mid-stream 429 or trailer -> overload signal, often accompanied by Retry-After; abrupt server termination -> 502/504; proxy cancel -> 499. Also a short paragraph about where Retry-After may appear (initial headers vs trailers) and how SDKs tend to surface it.

docs-bot: CI started for PR #900 — https://ci.internal.redwood/1400.

tyler: please add a concise resume example that avoids token duplication. customers keep trying to resend last N tokens which inflates cost.

claire: added a tiny "resumable cursor + idempotent tail" pattern and a short node snippet: ```js
// pseudo-node resumable stream
const resp = await client.stream({ prompt, headers: { 'x-stream-cursor': cursor } });
for await (const chunk of resp) {
  if (chunk.cursor <= lastCommitted) continue;
  output += chunk.text;
  lastCommitted = chunk.cursor;
}
```

marta: editorial: wrap header names in code spans (`x-stream-cursor`, `Retry-After`) and add a one-line note about Dedicated vs Hosted: Dedicated may queue requests instead of immediately returning 429.

claire: fixed casing and formatting; added 'Behavior by deployment' bullet linking to dedicated capacity docs and a short SDK migration note: "SDKs that previously auto-reconnected should offer explicit resume APIs or disable implicit reconnects for streaming endpoints."

raj: tiny nit: mention cost implications explicitly with a :warning: and crosslink to billing docs.

claire: added a short cost warning and crosslinks to error-ref 429, SDK retry docs, and billing page.

marta: LGTM with minor grammar tweaks. Merge when CI passes. :shipit:

